msgid "<keyword>xdm</keyword>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "display manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "desktop manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "login manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdm; provides a graphical interface that allows you to log in to a system. "
"It prompts for login (username) and password, authenticates the user and "
"starts a <quote>session</quote>. &kdm; is superior to &xdm;, the X Display "
"Manager, in a number of ways."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Start Guide"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is a quick start guide for users who fit the following pattern:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"X is configured and works with the command <command>startx</command> from "
"the commandline."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each user will generally only use a single window manager or desktop "
"environment, and does not change this choice very often, or is comfortable "
"editing a single text file in order to change their choice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This scenario will be sufficient for many environments where a single user "
"or several users normally boot the computer and log into their preferred "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting up a Default Session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create or open the file <filename>~/.xinitrc</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you already have a working <filename>~/.xinitrc</filename>, go to the "
"next step"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If one does not already exist, add a line to the <filename>~/.xinitrc</"
"filename> to start your preferred window manager or desktop environment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "For &kde; you should enter:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>startkde</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For other window managers or desktop environments, you should look in their "
"documentation for the correct command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "Make a link as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>ln</command> <option>-s</option> <parameter>~/.xinitrc "
"~/.xsession</parameter></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At this point, typing <userinput><command>startx</command></userinput> on "
"the commandline should start X, with a &kde; session. The next task is to "
"try &kdm;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>, type "
"<userinput><command>kdm</command></userinput> at the prompt."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You should see a login window, which is described more fully in <xref "
"linkend=\"login\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing your normal username and password in the fields provided, and leaving "
"<option>default</option> selected as the session type should now open a "
"&kde; session for your user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have other users to configure, you should repeat the procedure above "
"for each of them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a quick guide to getting up and running only. You probably will want "
"to customize &kdm; further, for example, to hide the names of the system "
"accounts, to allow further sessions, and much more. Please read through the "
"rest of this manual to find out how to do these things."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Login Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The user interface to &kdm; consists of dialog boxes. The main dialog box "
"contains:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Widgets allowing you to authenticate. When the \"classic\" authentication "
"method is chosen, these are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "A <guilabel>Username:</guilabel> field for you to enter your username."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "A <guilabel>Password:</guilabel> field for you to enter your password."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally) a list containing entries with the name and graphical image of "
"each user (for example, a digitized photograph). Clicking a list entry is "
"equivalent to typing the associated username into the <guilabel>Username:</"
"guilabel> field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally) a region to the right of or above the authentication area which "
"can be used to display either a static image or an analog clock."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <guibutton>Login</guibutton> button that validates the username/password "
"combination and attempts to start a session of the selected type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <guibutton>Menu</guibutton> button that opens an action menu with the "
"following items:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally) A <guimenuitem>Session Type</guimenuitem> item to choose the "
"type of session (desktop environment, window manager) to start. See <xref "
"linkend=\"different-window-managers-with-kdm\"/> to find out how to "
"configure different session types."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally) A <guimenuitem>Authentication Method</guimenuitem> item to "
"switch between different authentication methods like the classical username"
"+password, smartcard, biometry, &etc;. The actual authenticators are "
"combinations of <acronym>PAM</acronym> modules and matching frontend modules "
"(<quote>conversation plugins</quote>). See <xref linkend=\"option-"
"pluginslogin\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally on local displays) A <guimenuitem>Switch User...</guimenuitem> "
"item to switch between local sessions running on different virtual terminals "
"of this computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally on local displays) A <guimenuitem>Restart X Server</guimenuitem> "
"item that terminates the currently running &X-Server;, starts a new one and "
"displays the login dialog again. You can use this if the display content "
"seems to be broken somehow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally on remote displays) A <guimenuitem>Close Connection</"
"guimenuitem> item that closes the connection to the &XDMCP; server you are "
"currently connected to. If you got to this server through a host chooser, "
"this will bring you back to the chooser, otherwise it will only reset the &X-"
"Server; and bring up the login dialog again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally on local displays) A <guimenuitem>Remote Login</guimenuitem> "
"item that displays a host chooser dialog with &XDMCP; servers one can log "
"into remotely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally on local displays) A <guimenuitem>Console Mode</guimenuitem> "
"item that terminates graphical login and leaves you at the console. See "
"<xref linkend=\"option-consolettys\"/> and <xref linkend=\"option-servertty"
"\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally) A <guimenuitem>Shutdown...</guimenuitem> item that displays the "
"<guilabel>Shutdown</guilabel> dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Shutdown</guilabel> dialog box presents a set of buttons that "
"allow one of these actions to be executed:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "Turn Off Computer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shut the system down in a controlled manner, ready for power-down."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restart Computer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Shut the system down and reboot. For systems that use <application>Lilo</"
"application> or <application>Grub</application>, an optional drop down box "
"allows you to select a particular operating system to be used for the reboot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "Schedule..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, you may use it to enter a more complex shutdown "
"dialog. See <xref linkend=\"option-scheduledsd\"/> for details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pressing the <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> button returns to the main &kdm; "
"dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kdm;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter assumes that &kdm; is already up and running on your system, "
"and that you simply want to change its behavior in some way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &kdm; starts up, it reads its configuration from the folder <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/config/kdm/</filename> "
"(this may be <filename class=\"directory\">/etc/kde4/kdm/</filename> or "
"something else on your system)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main configuration file is &kdmrc;; all other files are referenced from "
"there and could be stored under any name anywhere on the system - but "
"usually that would not make much sense for obvious reasons (one particular "
"exception is referencing configuration files of an already installed &xdm; - "
"however when a new &kdm; is installed, it will import settings from those "
"files if it finds an already installed &xdm;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since &kdm; must run before any user is logged in, it is not associated with "
"any particular user. Therefore, it is not possible to have user-specific "
"configuration files; all users share the common &kdmrc;. It follows from "
"this that the configuration of &kdm; can only be altered by those users that "
"have write access to <filename>$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/config/kdm/"
"kdmrc</filename> (normally restricted to system administrators logged in as "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can view the &kdmrc; file currently in use on your system, and you can "
"configure &kdm; by editing this file. Alternatively, you can use the "
"graphical configuration tool provided by the &kcontrolcenter; (under "
"<menuchoice><guisubmenu>System Administration</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Login "
"Manager</guimenuitem></menuchoice>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The remainder of this chapter describes configuration of &kdm; via the "
"&kcontrolcenter; module, and the <link linkend=\"kdm-files\">next chapter</"
"link> describes the options available in &kdmrc; itself. If you only need to "
"configure for local users, the &kcontrolcenter; module should be sufficient "
"for your needs. If you need to configure remote logins, or have multiple "
"&kdm; sessions running, you will need to read on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: author
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Thomas.Tanghus; &Thomas.Tanghus.mail;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: author
#: index.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Steffen.Hansen; &Steffen.Hansen.mail;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: author
#: index.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Mike.McBride; &Mike.McBride.mail;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Login Manager &kcontrolcenter; Module"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this module, you can configure the &kde; graphical login manager, "
"&kdm;. You can change how the login screen looks, who has access using the "
"login manager and who can shutdown the computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All settings will be written to the configuration file &kdmrc;, which in its "
"original state has many comments to help you configure &kdm;. Using this "
"&kcontrolcenter; module will strip these comments from the file. All "
"available options in &kdmrc; are covered in <xref linkend=\"kdm-files\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The options listed in this chapter are cross referenced with their "
"equivalents in &kdmrc;. All options available in the &kcontrol; module are "
"also available directly in &kdmrc; but the reverse is not true."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to organize all of these options, this module is divided into "
"several sections: <link linkend=\"kdmconfig-appearance"
"\"><guilabel>Appearance</guilabel></link>, <link linkend=\"kdmconfig-font"
"\"><guilabel>Font</guilabel></link>, <link linkend=\"kdmconfig-background"
"\"><guilabel>Background</guilabel></link>, <link linkend=\"kdmconfig-shutdown"
"\"><guilabel>Shutdown</guilabel></link>, <link linkend=\"kdmconfig-users"
"\"><guilabel>Users</guilabel></link> and <link linkend=\"kdmconfig-"
"convenience\"><guilabel>Convenience</guilabel></link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can switch between the sections using the tabs at the top of the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are not currently logged in as a superuser, you will need to click "
"the <guibutton>Administrator Mode...</guibutton> Button. You will then be "
"asked for a superuser password. Entering a correct password will allow you "
"to modify the settings of this module."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid "Appearance"
msgstr "Aparéncia"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From this page you can change the visual appearance of &kdm;, &kde;'s "
"graphical login manager."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Greeting:</guilabel> is the title of the login screen. Setting "
"this is especially useful if you have many servers users may log in to. You "
"may use various placeholders, which are described along with the "
"corresponding key <link linkend=\"option-greetstring\"><option>GreetString</"
"option></link> in &kdmrc;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can then choose to show either the current system time, a logo or "
"nothing special in the login box. Make your choice in the radio buttons "
"labeled <guilabel>Logo area:</guilabel>. This corresponds to <link linkend="
"\"option-logoarea\"><option>LogoArea</option></link> in &kdmrc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you chose <guilabel>Show logo</guilabel> you can now choose a logo:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid "Drop an image file on the image button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the image button and select a new image from the image chooser "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not specify a logo, the default <filename>$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/"
"share/apps/kdm/pics/kdelogo.xpm</filename> will be displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Normally the login box is centered on the screen. Use the <guilabel>Position:"
"</guilabel> options if you want it to appear elsewhere on the screen. You "
"can specify the relative position (percentage of the screen size) for the "
"center of the login window, relative to the top left of the display, in the "
"fields labeled <guilabel>X:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Y:</guilabel> "
"respectively. These correspond to the key <link linkend=\"option-greeterpos"
"\"><option>GreeterPos</option></link> in &kdmrc;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While &kde;'s style depends on the settings of the user logged in, the style "
"used by &kdm; can be configured using the <guilabel>GUI Style:</guilabel> "
"and <guilabel>Color Scheme:</guilabel> options. These correspond to the keys "
"<link linkend=\"option-guistyle\"><option>GUIStyle</option></link> and <link "
"linkend=\"option-colorscheme\"><option>ColorScheme</option></link> in "
"&kdmrc; respectively."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below that, you have a drop down box to choose the language for your login "
"box, corresponding to setting <option>Language</option> in &kdmrc;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid "Font"
msgstr "Poliça"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From this section of the module you can change the fonts used in the login "
"window. Only fonts available to all users are available here, not fonts you "
"have installed on a per user basis."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select three different font styles from the drop down box "
"(<guilabel>General:</guilabel>, <guilabel>Failures:</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Greeting:</guilabel>). When you click on the <guibutton>Choose...</"
"guibutton> button a dialog appears from which you can select the new "
"characteristics for the font style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>General:</guilabel> font is used in all other places in the "
"login window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Failures:</guilabel> font is used when a login fails."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Greeting:</guilabel> font is the font used for the title "
"(Greeting String)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also check the box labeled <guilabel>Use anti-aliasing for fonts</"
"guilabel> if you want smoothed fonts in the login dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid "Background"
msgstr "Fons"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can change the desktop background which will be displayed before a "
"user logs in. The options are identical to those described in the <ulink url="
"\"help:/kcontrol/background/index.html\">background settings</ulink>, save "
"some that are not applicable to the &kdm; context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:510
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shutdown"
msgstr "Atudar"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allow Shutdown"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use this drop down box to choose who is allowed to shut down:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:516
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Nobody</guilabel>: No one can shutdown the computer using &kdm;. "
"You must be logged in, and execute a command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Everybody</guilabel>: Everyone can shutdown the computer using "
"&kdm;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Only Root</guilabel>: &kdm; requires that the <systemitem>root</"
"systemitem> password be entered before shutting down the computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can independently configure who is allowed to issue a shutdown command "
"for the <guilabel>Local:</guilabel> and <guilabel>Remote:</guilabel> users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands"
msgstr "Comandas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use these text fields to define the exact shutdown command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Halt:</guilabel> command defaults to <command>/sbin/halt</"
"command>. The <guilabel>Restart:</guilabel> command defaults to <command>/"
"sbin/reboot</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When <guilabel>Show boot options</guilabel> is enabled, &kdm; will on reboot "
"offer you options for the lilo boot manager. For this feature to work, you "
"will need to supply the correct paths to your <command>lilo</command> "
"command and to lilo's map file. Note that this option is not available on "
"all operating systems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:549
#, no-c-format
msgid "Users"
msgstr "Utilizaires"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"From here you can change the way users are represented in the login window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may disable the user list in &kdm; entirely in the <guilabel>Show Users</"
"guilabel> section. You can choose from:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:559
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show List"
msgstr "Visualizar la tièra"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:561
#, no-c-format
msgid "Only show users you have specifically enabled in the list alongside"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not check this box, no list will be shown. This is the most secure "
"setting, since an attacker would then have to guess a valid login name as "
"well as a password. It's also the preferred option if you have more than a "
"handful of users to list, or the list itself would become unwieldy."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid "Inverse selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to intead select a list of users that should <emphasis>not</"
"emphasis> be shown, and all other users will be listed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Independently of the users you specify by name, you can use the "
"<guilabel>System UIDs</guilabel> to specify a range of valid <acronym>UID</"
"acronym>s that are shown in the list. By default user id's under 1000, which "
"are often system or daemon users, and user id's over 65000, are not shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also enable the <guilabel>Sort users</guilabel> checkbox, to have "
"the user list sorted alphabetically. If this is disabled, users will appear "
"in the order they are listed in the password file. &kdm; will also "
"autocomplete user names if you enable the <guilabel>Autocompletion</"
"guilabel> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:592
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you choose to show users, then the login window will show images (which "
"you select), of a list of users. When someone is ready to login, they may "
"select their user name/image, enter their password, and they are granted "
"access."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you permit a user image, then you can configure the source for those "
"images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:600
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can configure the admin picture here, for each user on the system. "
"Depending on the order selected above, users may be able to override your "
"selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you choose not to show users, then the login window will be more "
"traditional. Users will need to type their username and password to gain "
"entrance. This is the preferred way if you have many users on this terminal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid "Convenience"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:614
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>convenience</guilabel> tab you can configure some options "
"that make life easier for lazy people, like automatic login or disabling "
"passwords."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please think more than twice before using these options. Every option in the "
"<guilabel>Convenience</guilabel> tab is well-suited to seriously compromise "
"your system security. Practically, these options are only to be used in a "
"completely non-critical environment, &eg; a private computer at home."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic Login"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Automatic login will give anyone access to a certain account on your system "
"without doing any authentication. You can enable it using the option "
"<guilabel>Enable Auto-login</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can choose the account to be used for automatic login from the list "
"labeled <guilabel>User:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Automatic login can be suppressed by pressing the Shift key immediately "
"after the &X-Server; switches to graphics mode and releasing it when &kdm;'s "
"hourglass cursor appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid "Password-Less Login"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this feature, you can allow certain users to login without having to "
"provide their password. Enable this feature using the <guilabel>Enable "
"Password-less logins</guilabel> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below this option you'll see a list of users on the system. Enable password-"
"less login for specific users by checking the checkbox next to the login "
"names. By default, this feature is disabled for all users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Again, this option should only be used in a safe environment. If you enable "
"it on a rather public system you should take care that only users with heavy "
"access restrictions are granted password-less login, &eg; <systemitem>guest</"
"systemitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also choose which user is <quote>preselected</quote> when &kdm; "
"starts. The default is <guilabel>None</guilabel>, but you can choose "
"<guilabel>Previous</guilabel> to have &kdm; default to the last successfully "
"logged in user, or you can <guilabel>Specify</guilabel> a particular user to "
"always be selected from the list. You can also have &kdm; set the focus to "
"the password field, so that when you reach the &kdm; login screen, you can "
"type the password immediately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:667
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Automatically login after X server crash</guilabel> option "
"allows you to skip the authentication procedure when your X server "
"accidentally crashed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:687
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring your system to use &kdm;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:689
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter assumes that your system is already configured to run the &X-"
"Window;, and that you only need to reconfigure it to allow graphical login."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:694
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting up &kdm;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The fundamental thing that controls whether your computer boots to a "
"terminal prompt (console mode) or a graphical login prompt is the default "
"runlevel. The runlevel is set by the program <application> <ulink url=\"man:"
"init\">/sbin/init</ulink></application> under the control of the "
"configuration file <filename>/etc/inittab</filename>. The default runlevels "
"used by different &UNIX; systems (and different &Linux; distributions) vary, "
"but if you look at <filename>/etc/inittab</filename> the start of it should "
"be something like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:705
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# Default runlevel. The runlevels used by RHS are:\n"
"# 0 - halt (Do NOT set initdefault to this)\n"
"# 1 - Single user mode\n"
"# 2 - Multiuser, without NFS\n"
"# 3 - Full multiuser mode\n"
"# 4 - unused\n"
"# 5 - X11\n"
"# 6 - reboot (Do NOT set initdefault to this)\n"
"\n"
"id:3:initdefault:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All but the last line of this extract are comments. The comments show that "
"runlevel 5 is used for X11 and that runlevel 3 is used for multi-user mode "
"without X11 (console mode). The final line specifies that the default "
"runlevel of the system is 3 (console mode). If your system currently uses "
"graphical login (for example, using &xdm;) its default runlevel will match "
"the runlevel specified for X11."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:714
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The runlevel with graphical login (&xdm;) for some common &Linux; "
"distributions is:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:718
#, no-c-format
msgid "5 for &RedHat; 3.x and later, and for &Mandrake;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:719
#, no-c-format
msgid "4 for Slackware"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid "3 for &SuSE;. 4.x and 5.x"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:723
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first step in configuring your system is to ensure that you can start "
"&kdm; from the command line. Once this is working, you can change your "
"system configuration so that &kdm; starts automatically each time you reboot "
"your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:728
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To test &kdm;, you must first bring your system to a runlevel that does not "
"run &xdm;. To do so, issue a command like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:731
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>/sbin/init <option>3</option></command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:733
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Instead of the number <option>3</option> you should specify the appropriate "
"runlevel for console mode on your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:736
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your system uses Pluggable Authentication Modules (<abbrev>PAM</abbrev>), "
"which is normal with recent &Linux; and &Solaris; systems, you should check "
"that your <abbrev>PAM</abbrev> configuration permits login through the "
"service named <literal>kde</literal>. If you previously used &xdm; "
"successfully, you should not need to make any changes to your <abbrev>PAM</"
"abbrev> configuration in order to use &kdm;. <filename>/etc/pam.conf</"
"filename> or <filename>/etc/pam.d/kde</filename>. Information on configuring "
"<abbrev>PAM</abbrev> is beyond the scope of this handbook, but <abbrev>PAM</"
"abbrev> comes with comprehensive documentation (try looking in <filename>/"
"usr/share/doc/*pam*/html/</filename>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:748
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now it's time for you to test &kdm; by issuing the following command:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kdm <option>-nodaemon</option></command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:753
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you get a &kdm; login dialog and you are able to log in, things are going "
"well. The main thing that can go wrong here is that the run-time linker "
"might not find the shared &Qt; or &kde; libraries. If you have a binary "
"distribution of the &kde; libraries, make sure &kdm; is installed where the "
"libraries believe &kde; is installed and try setting some environment "
"variables to point to your &kde; and &Qt; libraries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:761
#, no-c-format
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:763
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>export \n"
"<option>KDEDIR=<replaceable>/opt/kde</replaceable></option></command>\n"
"<command>export \n"
"<option>QTDIR=<replaceable>/usr/lib/qt4</replaceable></option></command>\n"
"<command>export \n"
"<option>PATH=<replaceable>$KDEDIR/bin:$QTDIR/bin:$PATH</replaceable></"
"option></command>\n"
"<command>export \n"
"<option>LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<replaceable>$KDEDIR/lib:$QTDIR/lib</replaceable></"
"option></command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:765
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are still unsuccessful, try starting &xdm; instead, to make sure that "
"you are not suffering from a more serious X configuration problem."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:769
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are able to start &kdm; successfully, you can start to replace "
"&xdm; by &kdm;. Again, this is distribution-dependent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:774
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For &RedHat;, edit <filename>/etc/inittab</filename>, look for this line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:776
#, no-c-format
msgid "x:5:respawn:/usr/X11/bin/xdm -nodaemon"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:777
#, no-c-format
msgid "and replace with:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:778
#, no-c-format
msgid "x:5:respawn:/opt/kde/bin/kdm"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:779
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tells <command>init</command>(8) to respawn &kdm; when the system is in "
"run level 5. Note that &kdm; does not need the <option>-nodaemon</option> "
"option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:784
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For &Mandrake;, the X11 runlevel in <filename>/etc/inittab</filename> "
"invokes the shell script <filename>/etc/X11/prefdm</filename>, which is set "
"up to select from amongst several display managers, including &kdm;. Make "
"sure that all the paths are correct for your installation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:791
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For &SuSE;, edit <filename>/sbin/init.d/xdm</filename> to add a first line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:794
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
". /etc/rc.config\n"
"DISPLAYMANAGER=kdm\n"
"export DISPLAYMANAGER"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:796
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For FreeBSD, edit <filename>/etc/ttys</filename> and find the line like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:798
#, no-c-format
msgid "ttyv8   \"/usr/X11R6/bin/xdm -nodaemon\"  xterm   off secure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:799
#, no-c-format
msgid "and edit it to this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:800
#, no-c-format
msgid "ttyv8   \"/opt/kde/bin/kdm\"  xterm   on secure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:803
#, no-c-format
msgid "Most other distributions are a variation of one of these."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:807
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At this stage, you can test &kdm; again by bringing your system to the "
"runlevel that should now run &kdm;. To do so, issue a command like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:811
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>/sbin/init <option>5</option></command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:813
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Instead of the number <option>5</option> you should specify the appropriate "
"runlevel for running X11 on your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:816
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The final step is to edit the <parameter>initdefault</parameter> entry in "
"<filename>/etc/inittab</filename> to specify the appropriate runlevel for "
"X11."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:820
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before you make this change, ensure that you have a way to reboot your "
"system if a problem occurs. This might be a <quote>rescue</quote> floppy-"
"disk provided by your operating system distribution or a specially-designed "
"<quote>rescue</quote> floppy-disk, such as <literal>tomsrtbt</literal>. "
"Ignore this advice at your peril."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:827
#, no-c-format
msgid "This usually involves changing the line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:828
#, no-c-format
msgid "id:3:initdefault:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:829
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>to</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:830
#, no-c-format
msgid "id:5:initdefault:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:832
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you reboot your system, you should end up with the graphical &kdm; "
"login dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:835
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this step is unsuccessful the most likely problem is that the environment "
"used at boot time differs from the environment that you used for testing at "
"the command line. If you are trying to get two versions of &kde; to co-"
"exist, be particularly careful that the settings you use for your "
"<envar>PATH</envar> and <envar>LD_LIBRARY_PATH</envar> environment variables "
"are consistent, and that the startup scripts are not over-riding them in "
"some way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:848
#, no-c-format
msgid "Supporting multiple window managers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:850
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdm; detects most available window manager and desktop environments when it "
"is run. Installing a new one should make it automatically available in the "
"&kdm; main dialog's <guimenuitem>Session Type</guimenuitem> submenu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:854
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have a very new window manager, or something that &kdm; does not "
"support, the first thing you should check is that the application to be run "
"is in the <envar>PATH</envar> and has not been renamed during the install "
"into something unexpected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:859
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the case is that the application is too new and not yet supported by "
"&kdm;, you can quite simply add a new session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:862
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The sessions are defined in <firstterm>.desktop</firstterm> files in "
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/apps/kdm/"
"sessions</filename>. You can simply add an appropriately named <literal role="
"\"extension\">.desktop</literal> file in this directory. The fields are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:869
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Desktop Entry]\n"
"Encoding=UTF-8 <lineannotation>This is fixed to <option>UTF-8</option> and\n"
"may be omitted</lineannotation>\n"
"Type=XSession <lineannotation>This is fixed to <option>XSession</option> "
"and\n"
"may be omitted</lineannotation>\n"
"Exec=<replaceable>executable name</replaceable> <lineannotation>Passed to\n"
"<command>eval exec</command> in a Bourne shell</lineannotation>\n"
"TryExec=<replaceable>executable name</replaceable> "
"<lineannotation>Supported\n"
"but not required</lineannotation>\n"
"Name=<replaceable>name to show in the &kdm; session list</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:871
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are also three <quote>magic</quote> types:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:875
#, no-c-format
msgid "default"
msgstr "defaut"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:877
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default session for &kdm; is normally &kde; but can be configured by the "
"system administrator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:884
#, no-c-format
msgid "custom"
msgstr "personalizat"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:886
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Custom session will run the user's ~/.xsession if it exists."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:892
#, no-c-format
msgid "failsafe"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:894
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Failsafe will run a very plain session, and is useful only for debugging "
"purposes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:902
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To override a session type, copy the .desktop file from the data dir to the "
"config dir and edit it at will. Removing the shipped session types can be "
"accomplished by <quote>shadowing</quote> them with .desktop files containing "
"Hidden=true. For the magic session types no .desktop files exist by default, "
"but &kdm; pretends they would, so you can override them like any other type. "
"I guess you already know how to add a new session type by now. ;-)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:913
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kdm; for Remote Logins (&XDMCP;)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:915
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&XDMCP; is the Open Group standard, the <quote>X Display Manager Control "
"Protocol</quote>. This is used to set up connections between remote systems "
"over the network."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:919
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&XDMCP; is useful in multiuser situations where there are users with "
"workstations and a more powerful server that can provide the resources to "
"run multiple X sessions. For example, &XDMCP; is a good way to reuse old "
"computers - a Pentium or even 486 computer with 16 Mb RAM is sufficient to "
"run X itself, and using &XDMCP; such a computer can run a full modern &kde; "
"session from a server. For the server part, once a single &kde; (or other "
"environment) session is running, running another one requires very few extra "
"resources."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:928
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"However, allowing another method of login to your machine obviously has "
"security implications. You should run this service only if you need to allow "
"remote X Servers to start login sessions on your system. Users with a single "
"&UNIX; computer should not need to run this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:937
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Topics"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:940
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Sockets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:942
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a feature you can use to remote-control &kdm;. It's mostly intended "
"for use by &ksmserver; and &kdesktop; from a running session, but other "
"applications are possible as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:946
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The sockets are &UNIX; domain sockets which live in subdirectories of the "
"directory specified by <option>FifoDir</option>=. The subdir is the key to "
"addressing and security; the sockets all have the file name "
"<filename>socket</filename> and file permissions <literal>rw-rw-rw-</"
"literal> (0666). This is because some systems don't care for the file "
"permission of the socket files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:953
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two types of sockets: the global one (dmctl) and the per-display "
"ones (dmctl-&lt;display&gt;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:956
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The global one's subdir is owned by root, the subdirs of the per-display "
"ones' are owned by the user currently owning the session (root or the logged "
"in user). Group ownership of the subdirs can be set via FifoGroup=, "
"otherwise it's root. The file permissions of the subdirs are rwxr-x--- "
"(0750)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:962
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The fields of a command are separated by tabs (<token>\\t</token>), the "
"fields of a list are separated by spaces, literal spaces in list fields are "
"denoted by <token>\\s</token>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:966
#, no-c-format
msgid "The command is terminated by a newline (<token>\\n</token>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:968
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The same applies to replies. The reply on success is <returnvalue>ok</"
"returnvalue>, possibly followed by the requested information. The reply on "
"error is an errno-style word (&eg; <returnvalue>perm</returnvalue>, "
"<returnvalue>noent</returnvalue>, &etc;) followed by a longer explanation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:975
#, no-c-format
msgid "Global commands:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:977
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>login</command> <option>display</option> (<parameter>now</"
"parameter> | <parameter>schedule</parameter>) <parameter>user</parameter> "
"<parameter>password</parameter> [session_arguments]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:981
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"login user at specified display. if <parameter>now</parameter> is specified, "
"a possibly running session is killed, otherwise the login is done after the "
"session exits. session_arguments are printf-like escaped contents for .dmrc. "
"Unlisted keys will default to previously saved values."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:990
#, no-c-format
msgid "Per-display commands:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:992
#, no-c-format
msgid "lock"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:994
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The display is marked as locked. If the &X-Server; crashes in this state, no "
"auto-relogin will be performed even if the option is on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:999
#, no-c-format
msgid "unlock"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1001
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Reverse the effect of <command>lock</command>, and re-enable auto-relogin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1006
#, no-c-format
msgid "suicide"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1008
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The currently running session is forcibly terminated. No auto-relogin is "
"attempted, but a scheduled \"login\" command will be executed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1015
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands for all sockets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1017
#, no-c-format
msgid "caps"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1019
#, no-c-format
msgid "Returns a list of this socket's capabilities:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: returnvalue
#: index.docbook:1023
#, no-c-format
msgid "<returnvalue>kdm</returnvalue>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1025
#, no-c-format
msgid "identifies &kdm;, in case some other DM implements this protocol, too"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:1030
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<returnvalue>list</returnvalue>, <returnvalue>lock</returnvalue>, "
"<returnvalue>suicide</returnvalue>, <returnvalue>login</returnvalue>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1033
#, no-c-format
msgid "The respective command is supported"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: returnvalue
#: index.docbook:1037
#, no-c-format
msgid "bootoptions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1039
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <command>listbootoptions</command> command and the <option>=</option> to "
"<command>shutdown</command> are supported"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: returnvalue
#: index.docbook:1044
#, no-c-format
msgid "shutdown &lt;list&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1046
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>shutdown</command> is supported and allowed for the listed users (a "
"comma separated list.) <returnvalue>*</returnvalue> means all authenticated "
"users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: returnvalue
#: index.docbook:1052
#, no-c-format
msgid "nuke &lt;list&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1054
#, no-c-format
msgid "Forced shutdown may be performed by the listed users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: returnvalue
#: index.docbook:1058
#, no-c-format
msgid "nuke"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1060
#, no-c-format
msgid "Forced shutdown may be performed by everybody"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: returnvalue
#: index.docbook:1064
#, no-c-format
msgid "reserve &lt;number&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1066
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Reserve displays are configured, and <returnvalue>number</returnvalue> are "
"available at this time"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:1072
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>list</command> [<parameter>all</parameter> | <parameter>alllocal</"
"parameter>]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1075
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Return a list of running sessions. By default all active sessions are "
"listed. if <parameter>all</parameter> is specified, passive sessions are "
"listed as well. If <parameter>alllocal</parameter> is specified, passive "
"sessions are listed as well, but all incoming remote sessions are skipped."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1080
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each session entry is a comma separated tuple of:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1082
#, no-c-format
msgid "Display or TTY name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1083
#, no-c-format
msgid "VT name for local sessions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1084
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Logged in user's name, empty for passive sessions and outgoing remote "
"sessions (local chooser mode)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1086
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Session type or <quote>&lt;remote&gt;</quote> for outgoing remote sessions, "
"empty for passive sessions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1088
#, no-c-format
msgid "A Flag field:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1089
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal>*</literal> for the display belonging to the requesting socket."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1091
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal>!</literal> for sessions that cannot be killed by the reqeusting "
"socket."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1096
#, no-c-format
msgid "New fields may be added in the future."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:1101
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>reserve</command> [<parameter>timeout in seconds</parameter>]"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Start a reserve login screen. If nobody logs in within the specified amount "
"of time (one minute by default), the display is removed again. When the "
"session on the display exits, the display is removed, too."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1107 index.docbook:1119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Permitted only on sockets of local displays and the global socket."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:1113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>activate</command> (<parameter>vt</parameter>|<parameter>display</"
"parameter>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Switch to a particular VT (virtual terminal). The VT may be specified either "
"directly (&eg; <parameter>vt3</parameter>) or by a display using it (eg; "
"<parameter>:2</parameter>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1125
#, no-c-format
msgid "listbootoptions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1127
#, no-c-format
msgid "List available boot options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1128
#, no-c-format
msgid "The return value contains these tokens:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1131
#, no-c-format
msgid "A list of boot options (as shown in &kdm; itself)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1134
#, no-c-format
msgid "The default boot option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1137
#, no-c-format
msgid "The current boot option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default and current option are zero-based indices into the list of boot "
"options. If either one is unset or not determinable, it is -1."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:1146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>shutdown</command> (<parameter>reboot</parameter> | "
"<parameter>halt</parameter>) [<parameter>=<replaceable>bootchoice</"
"replaceable></parameter>] (<parameter>ask</parameter>|<parameter>trynow</"
"parameter>|<parameter>forcenow</parameter>|<parameter>schedule</parameter>|"
"<parameter>start (<parameter>-1</parameter>|<parameter>end "
"(<parameter>force</parameter>|<parameter>forcemy</parameter>|"
"<parameter>cancel)</parameter>)</parameter>)</parameter>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1153
#, no-c-format
msgid "Request a system shutdown, either a reboot or a halt/poweroff."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An OS choice for the next boot may be specified from the list returned by "
"<command>listbootoptions</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Shutdowns requested from per-display sockets are executed when the current "
"session on that display exits. Such a request may pop up a dialog asking for "
"confirmation and/or authentication"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>start</parameter> is the time for which the shutdown is "
"scheduled. If it starts with a plus-sign, the current time is added. Zero "
"means immediately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>end</parameter> is the latest time at which the shutdown should "
"be performed if active sessions are still running. If it starts with a plus-"
"sign, the start time is added. -1 means wait infinitely. If end is through "
"and active sessions are still running, &kdm; can do one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1168
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>cancel</parameter> - give up the shutdown"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1170
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>force</parameter> - shut down nonetheless"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>forcemy</parameter> - shut down nonetheless if all active "
"sessions belong to the requesting user. Only for per-display sockets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>start</parameter> and <parameter>end</parameter> are specified in "
"seconds since the &UNIX; epoch."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>trynow</parameter> is a synonym for <parameter>0 0 cancel</"
"parameter>, <parameter>forcenow</parameter> for <parameter>0 0 force</"
"parameter> and <parameter>schedule</parameter> for <parameter>0 -1</"
"parameter>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>ask</parameter> attempts an immediate shutdown and interacts with "
"the user if active sessions are still running. Only for per-display sockets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:1189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>shutdown cancel</command> [<parameter>local</parameter>|"
"<parameter>global</parameter>}"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Cancel a scheduled shutdown. The global socket always cancels the currently "
"pending shutdown, while per-display sockets default to cancelling their "
"queued request."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: index.docbook:1199
#, no-c-format
msgid "shutdown status"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Return a list with information about shutdowns."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1202
#, no-c-format
msgid "The entries are a comma-separated tuples of:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(<returnvalue>global</returnvalue>|<returnvalue>local</returnvalue>) - "
"pending vs. queued shutdown. A local entry can be returned only by a per-"
"display socket."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1209
#, no-c-format
msgid "(<returnvalue>halt</returnvalue>|<returnvalue>reboot</returnvalue>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1210
#, no-c-format
msgid "start"
msgstr "començament"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1211
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>end</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1212
#, no-c-format
msgid "(\"ask\"|\"force\"|\"forcemy\"|\"cancel\")"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1213
#, no-c-format
msgid "Numeric user ID of the requesting user, -1 for the global socket."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1215
#, no-c-format
msgid "The next boot OS choice or \"-\" for none."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1217
#, no-c-format
msgid "New fields might be added later"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1224
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two ways of using the sockets:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Connecting them directly. FifoDir is exported as $<envar>DM_CONTROL</envar>; "
"the name of per-display sockets can be derived from $<envar>DISPLAY</envar>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By using the <command>kdmctl</command> command (&eg; from within a shell "
"script). Try <command>kdmctl</command> <option>-h</option> to find out more."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1238
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here is an example bash script <quote>reboot into FreeBSD</quote>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:1240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"if kdmctl | grep -q shutdown; then\n"
"  IFS=$'\\t'\n"
"  set -- `kdmctl listbootoptions`\n"
"  if [ \"$1\" = ok ]; then\n"
"    fbsd=$(echo \"$2\" | tr ' ' '\\n' | sed -ne 's,\\\\s, ,g;/freebsd/I{p;"
"q}')\n"
"    if [ -n \"$fbsd\" ]; then\n"
"      kdmctl shutdown reboot \"=$fbsd\" ask &gt; /dev/null\n"
"    else\n"
"      echo \"FreeBSD boot unavailable.\"\n"
"    fi\n"
"  else\n"
"    echo \"Boot options unavailable.\"\n"
"  fi\n"
"else\n"
"  echo \"Cannot reboot system.\"\n"
"fi"
msgstr ""

